# What the routes ask of the machine they run on, as data and one record of
# functions. A route turns a request into a `Job` (the heavy part: stage the
# source, run the compilers, run the program) and hands it to a `Host`, which
# decides where the job runs and under what limit, and whether an answer is
# kept. The runner has one host today, play/gate's: a job runs in a child
# process that holds a cross-process flock permit for as long as it runs, and
# no answer is written by a request (the process is the request, so there is
# nowhere to keep one); the deploy's sample answers are read.
#
# The record stayed when the second host, the long-lived JVM server's
# in-process Semaphore and answer cache, was removed with that server (K5 of
# docs/playground-native-runner-design.md). `keep_get` and `keep_put` are the
# answer store (play/answers): a serving process reads the answers a deploy
# computed for the samples and writes none (R2, 2026-10-21); a general cache
# written by requests would go behind the same two functions if the source
# digests in the access log ever showed programs coming back often enough to
# pay for one (ruling 4, 2026-10-19). The job is a closed set of cases and not a
# closure because it crosses into another process as a file.
use play/contract.{Outcome}
use play/exec.{ViewRaw, TileRaw}

## The heavy part of one request. `native` is whether `dawnc` may be used.
pub type Job =
  | JRun(code: String)
  | JCheck(code: String, native: Bool)
  | JView(code: String, native: Bool)
  | JTile(code: String, native: Bool)

## What a job came to. `JBroken` is a job that did not come back at all (the
## child died or wrote nothing): the route answers 500 with the message.
pub type JobResult =
  | JOutcome(outcome: Outcome)
  | JViewRaw(raw: ViewRaw)
  | JTileRaw(raw: TileRaw)
  | JBroken(message: String)

## `call(wait_secs, job)` runs the job once a permit is free, waiting up to
## `wait_secs` for one; None means the machine stayed saturated and the route
## answers 429. `keep_get` and `keep_put` are the answer store.
pub type Host = {
  call: fn(Int, Job) -> Option[JobResult] !io,
  keep_get: fn(String) -> Option[String] !io,
  keep_put: fn(String, String) -> Unit !io,
}

## The store of a host that keeps none.
pub fn no_keep_get(_key: String) -> Option[String] = None

pub fn no_keep_put(_key: String, _text: String) -> Unit = ()
